WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.960
So we are right
in the middle of our network meeting.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.760
All this wonderful people came here
to talk with us about Berlin

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.500
Science Week and to get to know each other
and us as a team.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.280
And this is a continuation
from our information session this morning,

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.800
which we held online and now really happy
to have everybody here

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.440
with us in the office.
I definitely recommend

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.920
joining Berlin Science Week
so you can grab different ideas.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.920
You could have a great exchange
with mind blowing

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.420
experts because

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.880
for renewed scientists in the field

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.280
and also just visitors who could inspire
you with their questions.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.040
It is not just about science,
but about the way science is communicated,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:52.400
which is usually what scientists are
struggling with because it's very nice.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.300
Yes, to do science,

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.760
but it's also very nice to be able
to communicate it to the general public.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.160
Well, in Science Week is a great space

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.660
to make networking between researchers
of different parts of the world.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.340
And we open the doors
of the Mexican embassy.

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:15.540
For those that are interested
in knowing the results of the cooperation

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:19.440
of the scientific relation
between Mexico and Germany.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.740
It's always important to bring societies,
science and art together.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:25.340
Yeah.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.040
Looking for a good co-creation.

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.240
We are also discussing whether we could

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.840
actually extend our partnership
into more creative

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:37.640
exploring ways of bringing arts
and science communities together.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.220
We just collecting the program right now.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:44.480
We have already quite some submissions,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:47.440
but still more to come,
hopefully from all of you.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:51.300
So please talk to us.

